"explanation": "In these assays Orava's dormancy is broken by one cue: exposure to a standardized smoke-derived chemical, followed by sustained moisture. Moisture alone supplies no cue, so spores given only water stay dormant through the five-day endpoint. Freeze-thaw cycles are not a substitute and have no direct germination effect, even with two full cycles and 48 hours of moisture afterward. Smoke followed by moisture is both necessary and sufficient. Because the cue was specified as smoke, a spore cohort receiving smoke without any freeze-thaw still germinates. The specified consequence is the smoke-then-moisture requirement. Recruitment on recently burned open ground, and cold affecting survival or timing, are plausible ecological interpretations rather than extra assay effects. Cold does not trigger dormancy break here.",
