}
}

raw.opening_A:
{
"explanation": "In this assay system, Orava spores remain dormant until they receive one specific cue, and sustained moisture only lets the cue take effect. Moisture alone supplies no cue, so a moisture-only cohort stays dormant at the five-day endpoint. The sampled cue here is the smoke-derived chemical exposure. A cohort given the complete smoke treatment and then 48 hours of sustained moisture breaks dormancy and germinates by the endpoint. Two full freeze-thaw cycles, even though they fit the species' alpine setting, are not the cue in this case. A freeze-thaw cohort followed by moisture therefore stays dormant, because nothing else is available to break dormancy. Light, nutrients, temperature, substrate and viability are permissive and identical across cohorts. So the outcome depends only on whether the smoke cue was delivered before the moisture period.",
"checks": {
"Q1": "FAIL",
"Q2": "FAIL",
"Q3": "PASS"
}
}

